<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<j:jelly xmlns:j="jelly:core">
  <p>Works like <code>bat</code>, but additionally writes the output of the commands to a file.</p>
  <pre>teeBat script: 'build.cmd', file: 'logs\\build.log'
def rc = teeBat(script: 'test.cmd', file: 'logs\\test.log', append: true, returnStatus: true)</pre>
  <ul>
    <li><code>file</code> (required): path relative to the workspace.</li>
    <li><code>append</code> (default: false): append instead of truncating the file.</li>
    <li><code>includeCommands</code> (default: false): echoed commands (<code>C:\ws&gt;cmd</code>) are always
      shown in the build log; set to true to write them to the file as well.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>All other parameters are passed to <code>bat</code> unchanged.</p>
</j:jelly>
